  "prompt": "You are a Senior Associate at a growth equity firm evaluating a potential investment in Tesla, Inc. (TSLA). Your Managing Director has asked you to prepare an investment memorandum to support the firm's investment committee decision on whether to initiate a position in Tesla. The committee is particularly interested in understanding Tesla's revenue trajectory, profitability trends, capital allocation efficiency, and the sustainability of its competitive advantages in the rapidly evolving electric vehicle and clean energy markets. Your analysis must be grounded in the attached financial data package and recent SEC filings.\n\nMaterials Provided:\n- The financial data package containing Tesla's XBRL-sourced financial metrics from Q2 2025 through Q1 2026, including revenue, profitability, balance sheet, and per-share data\n- A list of Tesla's recent SEC filings from April-May 2026\n\nTask Requirements:\n1. Prepare a professional investment memorandum in PDF format titled 'Investment Memo - Tesla, Inc. (TSLA)'.\n2. Structure the memo with the following sections:\n   - Executive Summary: Summarize the investment thesis, key financial highlights, and your overall recommendation in 2-3 paragraphs.\n   - Company Overview: Briefly describe Tesla's core business segments and market position based on available data.\n   - Financial Performance Analysis: Analyze revenue trends, gross profit margins, operating income, and net income across the provided quarterly and annual periods. Calculate and comment on key profitability ratios (e.g., gross margin, operating margin, net margin) for Q1 2026 and FY 2025.\n   - Balance Sheet and Capital Structure: Examine total assets, liabilities, stockholders' equity, and cash position. Calculate and discuss the debt-to-equity ratio and any notable changes in capital structure.\n   - Cash Flow and Liquidity Assessment: Based on the cash balances provided, discuss Tesla's liquidity position and any observable trends in cash reserves.\n   - Investment Risks and Mitigants: Identify the top 3-5 risks to the investment thesis, referencing specific financial metrics or trends from the data.\n   - Recommendation and Valuation Context: Provide a clear buy/hold/sell recommendation with supporting rationale. Discuss valuation considerations based on the earnings per share data.\n3. Focus your analysis on the period from Q2 2025 to Q1 2026, using FY 2025 data for annual context.\n4. All financial figures must be sourced from the provided data package. Do not invent or estimate any numbers not contained in the material.\n5. The memo should be 5-8 pages in length, with clear headings, subheadings, and professional formatting suitable for an investment committee presentation.",
